<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-RBQ-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-RBQ-002" ;
  triage:title "Task-escalation event read goes through TaskStore+spawn_blocking, not the in-scope AsyncTaskLedgerReader" ;
  triage:description "reminder_events() (:69-78) calls the synchronous TaskStore::list_task_events via run_blocking (herdr_queue_wake.rs:1019-1031) although an AsyncTaskLedgerReader with the identical list_task_events is live in the same pump tick (herdr_queue_wake.rs:435; used at read_due_task:503 and escalate_blocked:232) and is not threaded into record_task_outcome -> maybe_escalate_task (:597-659). Standing rule: task-ledger reads only via AsyncTaskLedgerReader; sprint-AX.6 documents the call as intentional but neither boundaries/atm-storage/task-store.toml nor async-task-ledger-reader.toml records a carve-out. Remediation (ruling, fenix 2026-09-06): option (a) — thread the existing AsyncTaskLedgerReader into maybe_escalate_task/reminder_events as escalate_blocked already does, and drop list_task_events from the TaskStore calls the AX.6 test enumerates. No boundary TOML change." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end_review" ;
  triage:category "ruthless-boundary-qa" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
